          "code": "DISPLAY_HIGH_VALUE_VAGUE_LINES",
          "id": "hv_display_high_value_vague_lines",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "hv_display_high_value_vague_lines_prompt",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are a UI rendering assistant. Your task is to transform the provided records into display markup only.\n\nInput data: {{$context.$nodes.FORMAT_HIGH_VALUE_VAGUE_LINES_FOR_DISPLAY.$output.result.formattedRows}}\n\nMass-return context:\n- requisitionLineDisplaysInPoolCsv: {{$context.$nodes.FORMAT_HIGH_VALUE_VAGUE_LINES_FOR_DISPLAY.$output.result.requisitionLineDisplaysInPoolCsv}}\n- reqLinesInPoolJson: {{$context.$nodes.FORMAT_HIGH_VALUE_VAGUE_LINES_FOR_DISPLAY.$output.result.reqLinesInPoolJson}}\n\nRequirements:\n1. If there are no input rows, output exactly: No data to display.\n2. If there are input rows, output exactly one valid oraInfoDisplay XML block with patternId=\"multiRecordWidget\". The only allowed output outside that block is the optional oraInsight described below.\n3. Do not output extra prose outside the display output.\n4. The oraInfoDisplay title, description, and subtitle must be empty.\n5. Set the multiRecordWidget description based only on the input rows:\n   - If at least one input row has reqsInPoolFlag equal to \"P\", set the multiRecordWidget description to exactly: \"Requisition lines on a purchase order can't be returned to requester\"\n   - Otherwise, leave the multiRecordWidget description empty.\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t   \n6. Preserve incoming row order exactly as provided.\n7. Render exactly 6 data columns in this order:\n   - Requisition - Line -> requisitionLineDisplay\n   - Description -> itemDescription\n   - Amount -> amountDisplay. Use amountDisplay exactly as provided.\n   - Requester -> requesterName\n   - Requisitioning BU -> requisitioningBUName\n   - Creation Date -> creationDateDisplay\n8. Do not render Reason, Buyer, vagueReason, reqsInPoolFlag, requisitionLineId, or action as visible columns.\n9. Values are preformatted; do not reformat numbers or dates.\n10. Add exactly one conditional action button per row using rows[].action only when reqsInPoolFlag is \"Y\":\n   - button text: \"Return\"\n   - command: ora.Invoke(\"returnToRequester\", { \"actionName\": \"returnToRequester\", \"requesterName\": requesterName, \"requisitionLineDisplay\": requisitionLineDisplay, \"reqLines\": [{ \"requisitionHeaderId\": requisitionHeaderId, \"requisitionLineId\": requisitionLineId, \"display\": requisitionLineDisplay, \"requesterName\": requesterName }] })\n   - For reqsInPoolFlag \"P\" and any other non-\"Y\" value, do not include an action for that row.\n11. Conditionally include exactly one oraInsight for mass return:\n   - If reqLinesInPoolJson is not an empty array, include one oraInsight with:\n     - title: \"Return Unprocessed Lines to Requester\"\n     - shortDescription: \"Return all unprocessed requisition lines shown to their requesters.\"\n     - actionText: \"Return Unprocessed Lines to Requester\"\n     - followUpCommand: ora.Invoke(\"returnToRequesterMassAction\", { \"actionName\": \"returnToRequesterMassAction\", \"requisitionLineDisplay\": \"<requisitionLineDisplaysInPoolCsv>\", \"reqLines\": <reqLinesInPoolJson> })\n     - Replace <requisitionLineDisplaysInPoolCsv> and <reqLinesInPoolJson> with the actual values from Mass-return context. <reqLinesInPoolJson> must remain a JSON array, not a quoted string.\n   - If reqLinesInPoolJson is an empty array, do not output this oraInsight.\n12. Keep row-level Return actions unchanged even when the mass-return oraInsight is present.\n\nUse multiRecordWidget cols and rows accordingly only when input rows exist. Ensure that the Return action button is rendered correctly for every eligible row by explicitly defining the action property for rows with reqsInPoolFlag \"Y\". Do not create any non-Return row action buttons."
            },
            {
              "id": "hv_display_high_value_vague_lines_systemPrompt",
              "name": "systemPrompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": ""
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Format High Value Vague Lines For Display",
            "returnType": "object",
            "sourceCode": "function isEmpty(value) {\n  return value == null || String(value).trim() === \"\";\n}\n\nfunction toFiniteNumber(value) {\n  if (value == null || value === \"\") return null;\n  const n = typeof value === \"number\" ? value : Number(value);\n  return Number.isFinite(n) ? n : null;\n}\n\nfunction sanitizeSeparator(value, fallback) {\n  if (typeof value !== \"string\") return fallback;\n  const text = value.trim();\n  return text !== \"\" ? text : fallback;\n}\n\nfunction sanitizeDatePattern(value) {\n  if (typeof value !== \"string\") return \"M/d/yyyy\";\n  const text = value.trim();\n  return text !== \"\" ? text : \"M/d/yyyy\";\n}\n\nfunction pad2(value) {\n  return String(value).padStart(2, \"0\");\n}\n\nfunction formatNumber(value, decimalSeparator, groupingSeparator, decimals) {\n  const n = toFiniteNumber(value);\n  if (n == null) return null;\n\n  const fixed = n.toFixed(decimals);\n  const negative = fixed.startsWith(\"-\");\n  const unsigned = negative ? fixed.slice(1) : fixed;\n  const parts = unsigned.split(\".\");\n  const integerPart = parts[0];\n  const fractionalPart = parts[1] ?? \"\";\n  const groupedInteger = integerPart.replace(/\\B(?=(\\d{3})+(?!\\d))/g, groupingSeparator);\n  const withDecimals = decimals > 0\n    ? groupedInteger + decimalSeparator + fractionalPart\n    : groupedInteger;\n\n  return negative ? \"-\" + withDecimals : withDecimals;\n}\n\nfunction formatDate(value, datePattern) {\n  if (isEmpty(value)) return \"-\";\n\n  const dateText = String(value).split(\"T\")[0];\n  const match = dateText.match(/^(\\d{4})-(\\d{2})-(\\d{2})$/);\n  if (!match) return dateText;\n\n  const year = match[1];\n  const month = Number(match[2]);\n  const day = Number(match[3]);\n  const tokens = {\n    yyyy: year,\n    YYYY: year,\n    yy: year.slice(-2),\n    YY: year.slice(-2),\n    MM: pad2(month),\n    M: String(month),\n    dd: pad2(day),\n    d: String(day)\n  };\n\n  return datePattern.replace(/yyyy|YYYY|yy|YY|MM|M|dd|d/g, (token) => tokens[token]);\n}\n\nfunction normalizeCurrencyCode(value) {\n  return String(value || \"\").trim().toUpperCase();\n}\n\nfunction toPrecision(value) {\n  const n = toFiniteNumber(value);\n  if (n == null || n < 0) return null;\n  return Math.trunc(n);\n}\n\nfunction buildCurrencyPrecisionMap(items) {\n  const map = {};\n  for (const item of Array.isArray(items) ? items : []) {\n    const currencyCode = normalizeCurrencyCode(item.CurrencyCode ?? item.currencyCode ?? item.Currency ?? item.currency);\n    const precision = toPrecision(item.Precision ?? item.precision ?? item.CurrencyPrecision ?? item.currencyPrecision);\n    if (currencyCode && precision != null) map[currencyCode] = precision;\n  }\n  return map;\n}\n\nfunction getCurrencyPrecision(currencyCode, currencyPrecisionMap, fallback) {\n  const precision = currencyPrecisionMap[normalizeCurrencyCode(currencyCode)];\n  return precision != null ? precision : fallback;\n}\n\nfunction buildMassReturnContext(rows) {\n  const rowsInPool = rows.filter((row) => String(row?.reqsInPoolFlag ?? \"\").trim().toUpperCase() === \"Y\");\n  const reqLinesInPoolJson = JSON.stringify(rowsInPool\n    .map((row) => ({\n      requisitionHeaderId: row.requisitionHeaderId,\n      requisitionLineId: row.requisitionLineId,\n      display: row.requisitionLineDisplay,\n      requesterName: row.requesterName,\n      requisitioningBU: row.requisitioningBUName\n    }))\n    .filter((row) => row.requisitionHeaderId != null && String(row.requisitionHeaderId).trim() !== \"\" && row.requisitionLineId != null && String(row.requisitionLineId).trim() !== \"\"));\n  const requisitionLineDisplaysInPoolCsv = rowsInPool\n    .map((row) => row.requisitionLineDisplay)\n    .filter((value) => value != null && String(value).trim() !== \"\")\n    .map((value) => String(value))\n    .join(\", \");\n\n  return {\n    reqLinesInPoolJson,\n    requisitionLineDisplaysInPoolCsv,\n  };\n}\n\nconst DISPLAY_ROW_LIMIT = 10;\nconst rows = $context.$nodes.FILTER_SEMANTIC_VAGUE_LINES.$output.result.selectedReqLines || [];\nconst displayRows = rows.slice(0, DISPLAY_ROW_LIMIT);\nif (rows.length === 0) {\n  return {\n    formattedRows: [],\n    total: 0,\n    reqLinesInPoolJson: \"[]\",\n    requisitionLineDisplaysInPoolCsv: \"\",\n    displayLimit: DISPLAY_ROW_LIMIT,\n    totalAvailable: 0,\n    formatting: {\n      skippedPreferenceFormatting: true\n    }\n  };\n}\n\nconst prefs = $context.$nodes.GET_USER_SESSION_PREFERENCES?.$output?.items?.[0];\nconst decimalSeparator = sanitizeSeparator(prefs?.DecimalSeparator, \".\");\nconst groupingSeparator = sanitizeSeparator(prefs?.GroupingSeparator, \",\");\nconst datePattern = sanitizeDatePattern(prefs?.DateFormat);\nconst currencyPrecisionMap = buildCurrencyPrecisionMap($context.$nodes.GET_CURRENCIES?.$output?.items);\nconst defaultCurrencyPrecision = 2;\nconst formattedRows = displayRows.map((row) => {\n  const displayAmount = toFiniteNumber(row.displayLineAmount) ?? toFiniteNumber(row.lineAmount);\n  const currency = row.displayCurrency || row.currencyCode || row.targetCurrency || \"USD\";\n  const amountPrecision = getCurrencyPrecision(currency, currencyPrecisionMap, defaultCurrencyPrecision);\n  const amountText = formatNumber(displayAmount, decimalSeparator, groupingSeparator, amountPrecision);\n\n  const formattedRow = {\n    ...row,\n    requisitionHeaderId: row.requisitionHeaderId,\n    requisitionLineDisplay: isEmpty(row.requisitionLineDisplay) ? \"-\" : row.requisitionLineDisplay,\n    itemDescription: isEmpty(row.itemDescription) ? \"-\" : row.itemDescription,\n    amountDisplay: amountText == null ? \"-\" : amountText + \" \" + currency,\n    amountPrecision,\n    requesterName: isEmpty(row.requesterName) ? \"-\" : row.requesterName,\n    requisitioningBUName: isEmpty(row.requisitioningBUName) ? \"-\" : row.requisitioningBUName,\n    creationDateDisplay: formatDate(row.creationDate, datePattern),\n    buyerName: isEmpty(row.buyerName) ? \"-\" : row.buyerName,\n    vagueReason: isEmpty(row.vagueReason) ? \"-\" : row.vagueReason\n  };\n  return formattedRow;\n});\nconst massReturnContext = buildMassReturnContext(formattedRows);\n\nreturn {\n  formattedRows,\n  total: formattedRows.length,\n  totalAvailable: rows.length,\n  displayLimit: DISPLAY_ROW_LIMIT,\n  ...massReturnContext,\n  formatting: {\n    decimalSeparator,\n    groupingSeparator,\n    datePattern,\n    defaultCurrencyPrecision,\n    currencyPrecisionMap\n  }\n};"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "hv_display_high_value_vague_lines"
          },
          "code": "FORMAT_HIGH_VALUE_VAGUE_LINES_FOR_DISPLAY",
          "id": "hv_format_for_display",
